ALAMO LITERATURE CIRCULATION IS MORE THAN USA TODAY, THE NEW
YORK TIMES, L.A. TIMES AND MANY OTHER NATIONAL PUBLICATIONS
COMBINED

                           ALWAYS PRAY
                                By
                            Tony Alamo


I John 3:9 states, "Whosoever is born" (again) "of God doth
not commit sin; for His seed remaineth in him:" (He will
remain sanctified, bathing daily in the blood of Christ1 and
washing himself daily in the cleansing Word of God.2)  "and he
cannot sin, because he is born" (the second time3) "of God,"
(born of God's Spirit4, which means born by belief in the
affirmations written in God's Holy Word, which is Spirit and
Life for us5). A new life is introduced into the sinner who
believes, causing the sinner to pass out of the kingdom of
darkness into the kingdom of light, out of death into life,
leading to righteousness and holiness, into the life, thus
purifying it and cleansing it each and every day. Jesus said,
"The Words that I speak unto you, they are Spirit, and they
are Life."6  "In this the children of God are manifest, and
the children of the devil."7

When we are without sin, without failure, our conscience
cannot convict us of sin because sin is not there any more.  A
true Christian will diligently search the Scriptures to find
more of God's commandments to keep, that he may be blessed
with more power, more peace, more prosperity, and more
assurance of life from God.8

The true Christian is one who will, as a habit of life, first
contact God in prayer on all things, and exercise meticulous
care in keeping all of God's commandments.9 It is this person
who God abides in, and who abides in God.10 This person knows
by experience that God abides in him, because the Holy Spirit
living inside him is his source of life witness, which is
God, our Life and Comforter.11 The Holy Ghost genders in us
the assurance that He, the Father, and His Son abide in us12
(who have been born the second time of the Spirit), who then
will continue keeping all of God's commandments.13

Jesus gave His disciples an illustration of this.  His
objective was to teach them, as well as us today, the most
important message; that it is a necessity to pray at all times
and to not lose courage if they, as well as all humanity who
choose Christ, want to remain in the status of the second born
of the Spirit and receive all of God's boundless, abundant
blessings.

To illustrate this, Jesus began His parable thus: "A certain
judge there was in a certain city.  God he did not fear, and man
he did not respect.  Now, there was a widow in that city, and she
kept on coming to him at recurring intervals, saying, Protect me
by an equitable administration  of justice from my opponent in a
lawsuit. And he kept on being unwilling to do so for a
considerable time.  However, afterward he said in himself,
Although God I do not fear or man respect, at least because this
widow is continually bringing me trouble" (pestering me) "I will
see that justice is done her in order that lest by her continual
pleading finally she may be driving me mad.  And the Lord said,
Hear what the unjust judge is saying.  And God, shall He not most
assuredly accomplish the vindication of His chosen-out ones who
are crying aloud to Him day and night, exacting justice in their
behalf, even though He is long-suffering in their case [that of
the enemies of His chosen-out ones].  I am saying to you, He will
exact justice in their behalf speedily. Yet, the Son of Man
having come, will He find the aforementioned kind of faith on the
earth [a faith which keeps on pleading in prayer such as that
exemplified by the persistence of the widow with regard to the
judge]?"14 When Christ comes, will He find any on earth who do
not doubt Him, who will be constantly praying in faith for the
perfect will of our heavenly Father, for His divine guidance,
which saves us from all disaster and miseries? When Christ
returns, will He find any who zealously keep all His
commandments, who serve Him with all their heart, soul, mind, and
strength as the first and most important commandment proclaims we
must?15 We are to cast all of our cares upon Him continuously in
prayer, for He careth for us.16

When we pray, we are commanded to never doubt or worry. We are
not to dwell primarily on our sicknesses, our diseases, our
infirmities, our perils, our trials and tribulations, or any of
our other needs.  Instead, we are to put on the mind of Christ,17
which means we must be calm and sure of God, completely trusting
Him.  We must concentrate on His all-powerful and most wonderful
deliverances recorded in His divine Word, trusting He will give
us "exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think,
according to the power that worketh in us."18 This is THE DIVINE
LAW, GOD'S DIVINE LAW, and it works every time, all the time if
we keep holiness and righteousness the law of habit.

God is all-powerful.  God does not permit the soul who doubts to
have anything.  The Apostle James, by the Holy Spirit, stated "If
any of you lack wisdom," (the fear of God19) "let him ask of God"
(by praying always to God), "that giveth to all men liberally,"
(the fear of God, wisdom) "and upbraideth not; and it shall be
given him.  But let him ask" (pray) "in faith, nothing wavering"
(not at all doubting).  "For he that wavereth" (doubts) "is like
a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.  For let not
that man think that he shall receive any thing of the Lord.  A
double minded man" (a doubter of God's Word) "is unstable in all
his ways."20 If you want God's answer, get in your chamber of
continuous prayer and forever call on Him in unwavering faith.

The Apostle James also stated, "Ye lust," (ye want) "and have
not: ye kill," (hate your brother without a cause and  don't love
your neighbor as the second most important commandment says we
must.21 You do not love your enemies as Jesus commanded we must,
overcoming evil by doing that which is good, which God tells
us.)22 "and desire to have, and cannot obtain:" (because you are
out of God's will) "ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye
ask not"23 (you pray not always in faith that God will hear you
and answer you).24

We must not permit ourselves to get off God's freeway of
righteousness, sanctification, to doubt, to not believe God. We
must believe the command of Jesus.  We must, with faith, "PRAY
ALWAYS,"25 that we may stay in His unlimited, victorious power of
the second born and receive all the gifts in the treasury of
God's faithful and true promises.  We are saved, healed, and
delivered by our faith in God's all-powerful abilities.  His
all-powerful, unlimited abilities are affirmed in others like
ourselves throughout His holy Word.  He will do the same for us
as He did for them if we do all that He says, which means if we
will maintain the restoration of His divine image in us through
the Holy Spirit and sanctification to "PRAY ALWAYS," and trust
Him always as they did.  This will be confirmed constantly in our
daily lives, as it was in theirs.

We are commanded to completely cast away and forsake all of our
anxieties, doubts, and worries, as well as to eradicate all
thoughts of limitation, poverty or lack. There is no limitation
to what God can do. With God, there are no bounds. If we do our
part, we can rely on God positively doing His part. His
mysterious forces will come to your aid behind the scenes, and
all that you have prayed for will soon materialize. In this you
may be fully confident. Everything that you desire according to
God's will can be obtained by keeping God's commandments,
especially the main one, "PRAY ALWAYS," "doubting nothing."26

Things you may want but not need can lead you astray from God's
purposes, causing you to miss God's ultimate good reward
(Heaven). Make God's will your will and your sole objective, so
that your reward will not be the eternal evil reward (Hell).

By reading (hearing) the affirmations recorded in God's holy
Word, we receive an increase of our faith, which genders in us
more of God's powerful Holy Spirit, divine peace, joy, and full
abundance.27 The God of the Old Testament, in the person of
Christ, will live in your human flesh through the Holy Spirit,
just as He did in the flesh of incarnate Christ Himself two
thousand years ago.  In this we know Him, not only from the
divine Word, but by experiencing His power living and abiding
within us, which always occurs in everyone who is second born of
the Holy Ghost and continues on a daily basis in His will.  We
receive the greatest peace, joy, courage, and calm possible when
we trustingly realize that God's divine Word is true. The laws of
God for acquiring salvation, healing, and deliverance positively
work.28

When we pray, the former and present deeds that God has  done and
continuously does must be meditated and concentrated upon,
constantly read, keeping the affirmations of His power and mercy
before us as the pupil of our eyes.29 We are to harness or unite
our will to God's will in constant prayer, that we may receive of
His mercy, His unlimited power and benefits.  We must, by
righteousness and holiness in our newly restored life, elevate
ourselves up to His standards by obeying all the commandments of
Christ. "Take My yoke" (My harness) "upon you, and learn of Me;
for I am meek and lowly" (obedient to the Father) "in heart: and
ye shall find rest unto your souls. For My yoke" (My harness of
obedience to the Father) "is easy, and My burden is light."30

God's Word commands that we are not to be "unequally yoked"
(harnessed) "together with unbelievers" (the disobedient to the
Father).31 That's why, if we believe, we will yoke up with His
will and none other.  Again, "to do Thy will, O God."32 It is
God's will to possess all power. If it were not God's will to
possess all power, He would not possess all the power in Heaven
and Earth. Jesus said, "All power is given unto Me in Heaven and
in Earth."33 THIS POSITIVELY IS HIS WILL. This fact is easily
affirmed in God's Word by the multitude of recorded, magnificent,
all-powerful testimonies,34 His all-power, and the manifestation
of His power with all of those living today who trust in Him.35

Jesus is everything.  He said, "I am THE WAY, THE TRUTH, AND THE
LIFE:" (what could be more?) "NO MAN COMETH UNTO THE FATHER, BUT
BY ME."36 This truthful and all-powerful statement eliminates all
other ways into Heaven. Anyone trying to sneak or creep into
Heaven by any other person, any other way, than through Christ,
